.TH "GLESHA-STATE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-state \- move local state from the legacy location
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha state\fR migrate [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move local state from the legacy location, USER_CONFIG/glesha/state\-v2, to the current one: the \-\-state\-dir directory, the [catalog] directory setting, or DATA/glesha/state.
.PP
Archives are moved without re\-encryption. A destination that already holds state is never merged into; choose an empty one with \-\-state\-dir. No cloud access is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha state migrate
glesha state migrate \-\-state\-dir /srv/glesha
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-list (1)
